/-!
# Effective real SNC fourfold adjoints have log minimal models

Let `π : X ⟶ Z` be a morphism of projective complex varieties with `X` smooth of dimension four,
and let `K_X` be a canonical divisor of `X`. Let `B` be a real boundary (coefficients in
`[0, 1]`) and `M ≥ 0` a real divisor such that `B + M` has simple normal crossing support and
`K_X + B ≡_Z M`. Suppose that `B` contains an effective ample `ℚ`-divisor `A` none of whose
components lies in `⌊B⌋` or in `Supp M`. Then `(X/Z, B)` has a log minimal model `(Y/Z, B_Y)`:
a normal projective `ℚ`-factorial dlt pair with a birational map `X ⤏ Y` over `Z`, where `B_Y`
is the strict transform of `B` plus the prime divisors of `Y` exceptional over `X`, such that
`K_Y + B_Y` is nef over `Z` and the comparison of adjoints on a common resolution is effective,
exceptional over `Y`, and positive along every prime divisor of `X` contracted on `Y`.

## Main results

* `MMP.Fourfold.exists_isRealLogMinimalModel_of_isSNC`: the existence of the log minimal model.

## Implementation notes

* The joint snc support of `B` and `M` is the snc condition on `B + M`: both are effective, so
  the prime divisors with nonzero coefficient in `B + M` are those of `B` and those of `M`.
* "`A` is a component of `B`" is read as `A ≤ B`, the components of `A` having coefficient
  `< 1` in `B` and `0` in `M`.
* The log minimal model is `MMP.Fourfold.IsRealLogMinimalModel`, which already carries the
  projectivity, `ℚ`-factoriality and dlt condition of the model.

## References

* [C. Birkar, *Existence of log canonical flips and a special LMMP*][BirkarLC]
-/

@[expose] public section

